<title>EL SALVADOR: EL SALVADOR JULY CONSUMER PRICES RISE 0.78 PERCENT.</title>
<headline>EL SALVADOR JULY CONSUMER PRICES RISE 0.78 PERCENT.</headline>
<dateline>SAN SALVADOR, El Salvador 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumer inflation in El Salvador rose 0.78 percent in July compared with June, the government said on Monday.</p>
<p>Inflation was 0.39 percent in June.</p>
<p>Accumulated inflation for the first seven months of the year was 3.39 percent, compared with a rise of 6.7 percent in the same period a year earlier, the government's statistics agency said.</p>
<p>((--El Salvador newsroom +503 223-1394))</p>
